## Problem 7 — metrics without a cardinality explosion

Edit `ex7/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface Registry {
  counter(name: string, labels?: Record<string, string>, by?: number): void;
  gauge(name: string, value: number, labels?: Record<string, string>): void;
  observe(name: string, value: number, labels?: Record<string, string>): void;
  seriesCount(): number;
  droppedSeries(): number;
  expose(): string;      // Prometheus text format
}

export function createRegistry(options: {
  buckets: readonly number[];
  maxSeries: number;
}): Registry
```

Requirements:

- a *series* is a metric name plus a canonical rendering of its labels, with
  keys sorted so `{a,b}` and `{b,a}` are one series, not two;
- once `seriesCount()` reaches `maxSeries`, a **new** series is refused and
  `droppedSeries()` increments; existing series keep working;
- `observe` records into a cumulative histogram over `options.buckets` plus
  `+Inf`, and tracks `_sum` and `_count`;
- `expose()` emits Prometheus text: `name{label="value"} number` per line,
  histograms as `name_bucket{le="0.1"}`, `name_sum`, `name_count`, with lines
  sorted for stable output.

```ts
const r = createRegistry({ buckets: [0.1, 0.5, 1], maxSeries: 100 });
r.counter("http_requests_total", { route: "/orders/:id", status: "200" });
r.observe("http_duration_seconds", 0.3, { route: "/orders/:id" });
r.expose();
// http_duration_seconds_bucket{le="0.1",route="/orders/:id"} 0
// http_duration_seconds_bucket{le="0.5",route="/orders/:id"} 1
// ...
```

